So, during this await, two delivery handles can be outside stable manager ownership: the older future has already been popped from the manager, and the new future has not yet been pushed into the manager. If the parent sink future is dropped there, both handles are dropped without any surviving manager state that can observe success/failure or gate truncation.

This cancellation is reachable because the sink executor races the current sink-consuming future against rebuild/config-update messages. If the rebuild/config branch wins, the current consume future is dropped:

