## Summary

On Windows, a `node:net` `createServer()` listening on a named pipe path fires `'connection'` for the first client, but **never for subsequent clients** after the first one disconnects. The kernel-level `CreateFile` on the client side still succeeds (client-side `'connect'` fires), so a client can be left waiting forever for a server-side reader that Deno never installs.

Works on Deno 2.7.11 and on Linux/macOS Unix sockets. Broken on Deno 2.7.12 and 2.7.13.

