It's impossible to use `DelayQueue` in a loop with `select!`, because the `select!` macros requires all streams to be `fuse`d, but `DelayQueue` returns `Ready(None)` if it no contains any scheduled item. It "breaks" a `FusedStream`.

That's good to have `always_pending` option that will never return `Ready(None)` and a `DelayQueue` instance can be used with `fuse` wrapper without drawbacks.

```rust
