### Motivation
Feedback from users that when the shell disconnects/ reconnects their session variables get reset. They also find the Notice about the connection disrupt/ MZ version block to be disruption and pollutes shell history upon reconnection

Fixes [CNS-29](https://linear.app/materializeinc/issue/CNS-29/shell-reconnects-interrupts-the-query-workflow) and [CNS-28](https://linear.app/materializeinc/issue/CNS-28/session-variables-get-reset-on-shell-reconnect)

### Description
- Added the callback `getSessionVariables`  to read the current session variables and reflect that on reconnect
- When the shell reconnects, I have added a toast to show "reconnecting.." and "connected" instead of a server notice in the shell history. I added a "retry" button for the queries in-flight when the connection is established again


**WebsocketConnectionManager:**

- Added `hasEverConnected` and `isReconnectionHandshake` fields to `ReconnectionState`, published via the Jotai atom so components can react to connection lifecycle transitions
- Added` clearReconnectionHandshake()` method to suppress server notices (welcome banners) during a timed window after reconnection
- Added `getSessionVariables `callback option so each reconnect uses the latest cluster/schema/search_path instead of stale values from construction time
- Wrapped `reconnect()` in try/catch so a throwing WebSocket constructor doesn't break the retry chain

**ShellWebsocketProvider:**

- `onOpen:` Resets the FSM on reconnection (using hasEverConnected from the atom) so the shell doesn't stay stuck in "Command is processing"
- ` onClose:` Marks in-flight commands as interrupted before stopping the FSM, resets FSM state to initialState, only commits a history notice on the very first connection failure (toasts handle subsequent disconnects)
- `ReadyForQuery`: Triggers clearReconnectionHandshake() to start the notice-suppression window


**New: useShellConnectionToasts hook:**

- Reactive hook that watches reconnectionStateAtom transitions to show "Connection interrupted" / "Reconnected" toasts

**HistoryOutput:**

Added interrupted flag to **CommandOutput** type


