### Describe the bug

A prepared statement can have types in the query:
```
select $1::int4 + $2::int8;
```
Or it can be specified as part of the API / extended query protocol:
```
select $1 + $2; -- API specifies [int4, int8]
```

In the latter case, when RisingWave actually executes a query with arguments, for example `[4, 5]`, the current version executes `select 4 + 5;` and returns `9` as `int4`, effectively ignoring the specified types. As the prepared statement is expecting an `int8`, the client would not be able to deserialize the query result when passed in BINARY format. (TEXT format may work because `int4` serialized in TEXT can also be deserialized as `int8`, but this is still a type mismatch.)

### To Reproduce

```
// cargo add postgres
use postgres::{Client, NoTls};
use postgres::types::Type;

fn main() {
    let mut client = Client::connect("host=localhost port=4566 dbname=dev user=root", NoTls).unwrap();

    let prepared = client.prepare_typed(
        "select $1 + $2",
        &[Type::INT4, Type::INT8],
    ).unwrap();

    let rows = client.query(
        &prepared,
