* I'm working on making an architectural change to `tokio-signal` where a single, long-lived future is spawned on an executor.
* This future (or the Driver) broadcasts any pending signals caught by a signal handler onto any leaf futures which are interested in a particular signal
* Once all signal listerners go away, we attempt to wake up the Driver so that it can resolve and unblock the executor
* The Driver is resurrected as needed if it has gone away on its own **OR** the event loop which drives it is dropped
